# Frontend React Guidelines

The frontend is a React 18 application in [frontend/src/](mdc:frontend/src/).

## Main Component

Entry point: [frontend/src/index.js](mdc:frontend/src/index.js)
Main App: [frontend/src/App.js](mdc:frontend/src/App.js)

## Key Features

### State Management
- Uses React hooks: `useState`, `useEffect`
- State includes: entries, form data, loading, error, success messages
- Speech recognition integration for voice input

### API Integration
```javascript
const API_URL = process.env.REACT_APP_API_URL || 'http://localhost:5000';
```
- Uses axios for HTTP requests
- All API calls go through backend API

### Speech Recognition
- Web Speech API integration
- Continuous and interim results enabled
- English (en-US) language setting
- Automatic transcript appending to content

### User Experience
- Loading states for async operations
- Success/error message display
- Confirmation dialogs for destructive actions
- Real-time AI status indicator

## Component Structure

Single-page application with:
- Header with title and description
- AI status indicator
- Journal entry form
- Previous entries list
- Entry actions (AI analysis, delete)

## Styling

CSS file: [frontend/src/index.css](mdc:frontend/src/index.css)
- Gradient background (#667eea to #764ba2)
- Card-based layout
- Button hover effects and animations
- Responsive design
- Color-coded UI elements

## Best Practices

- Keep components functional
- Use proper error handling in async operations
- Implement loading states for better UX
- Use semantic HTML
- Maintain accessibility standards
